    <description>Maximum air temperatures above 32 °C. Possible complications, especially in transport, livestock production, and the energy industry. Possible deformation of rails in rail transport, damage to poor quality roads, particularly those exposed to sunlight. The need for intensive cooling of enclosed halls (livestock production, industry, logistics, etc.). Higher load on energy infrastructure.</description>
